globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN=Object.assign(globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN||{},{
'兄弟':{
'紫微':{title:`A little king lives in the family`,story:`With Zi Wei in your Siblings palace, your brothers and sisters or close peers tend to be opinionated and capable, with a natural air of authority. Your relationship is more about mutual respect than clinging to each other. They will step in at crucial moments, but they are also used to advising you by their own standards.`,scenes:[`When you change jobs, your older brother or sister asks about salary and title first, then gives you a full "here's what I think you should do" analysis.`,`Dividing up work with a business partner, you may find they always want the final say, even scheduling meetings around their habits.`],advice:`Thank them properly when you accept their help, but keep the final decision in your own hands.`},
'紫微·天府':{title:`Two grand houses side by side`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tian Fu together in your Siblings palace, your siblings or close peers are usually steady and good with money, a backstop you can lean on for each other. You each have your own views, keep a respectful distance and rarely interfere. When it comes to cash flow, family or old friends are often your last safety net.`,scenes:[`When you are suddenly short on a down payment, one call to your sister is enough; she asks what it is for and lends it to you.`,`You may handle your parents' house together with your brother; you disagree, but you both stick to the rules.`],advice:`Whether it is a loan or a division of tasks, write it down and spell it out; that is how solid relationships last.`},
'紫微·天相':{title:`A family contract built on trust`,story:`Your siblings or peers care about courtesy and fairness, and your relationship looks dignified and orderly. When something comes up in the family, everyone tends to sort it out by the rules, and you are often expected to keep the bigger picture in mind. The help: someone is always willing to step up and handle things. The friction: everyone worries about face, so honest words are hard to say.`,scenes:[`For holiday gifts to the family, you agree in the group chat on how much each person contributes before anyone acts.`,`Partnering with a peer, you may negotiate very polished terms, yet nobody speaks up first about what they are unhappy with.`],advice:`Set face aside and make a habit of regular honest talks; your relationship will feel more solid.`},
'紫微·破軍':{title:`Princes who each lead their own troops away`,story:`Your siblings or peers have strong personalities and love starting new things, each on their own path, and your relationship goes through big swings: close for a while, then distant. Partnerships with them often start with passion and change course midway. Money comes and goes fast, so keep some extra room.`,scenes:[`Your younger brother suddenly quits his job to start a business and asks you to join; you are tempted and worried about your savings at the same time.`,`You and a peer may fall out over a family matter and stop speaking, then six months later meet for dinner as if nothing happened.`],advice:`Agree on an exit plan before working together, and keep feelings and business separate, so nobody gets hurt too badly.`},
'紫微·七殺':{title:`Two generals sharing one long table`,story:`Your siblings or peers are forceful, decisive and quick to act, so there is little lukewarmness between you and a lot of directness. When you disagree, neither gives way, but if an outsider picks on you, they are the first to stand up for you. Partnerships work best when each runs their own area, not when every decision is made together.`,scenes:[`On a family trip, you and your brother each planned an itinerary, and you are still arguing over where to go first at the rest stop.`,`When a friend who is also a colleague messes up, you might take the blame for them on the spot and only scold them privately afterward.`],advice:`Be clear about who manages what, and the energy you spend butting heads turns into mutual support.`},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:`A lively family banquet with all the trimmings`,story:`Your siblings or peers are multitalented, enjoy the good life and know lots of people, so time with them is always lively and fun. Your bond is often kept alive through food, outings and shared interests. Friction usually comes from spending habits, or a quiet contest over who is doing better.`,scenes:[`Your sister always picks the restaurant for family dinners, and it is always the kind with a queue or a booking weeks ahead.`,`You and a close friend might both get hooked on camping, buy more and more gear, and lose track of who paid for what.`],advice:`Have fun together, but each pay your own share in full, and comparison will not drag your relationship down.`},
'天機':{title:`A band of strategists full of ideas`,story:`Your siblings or close peers are clever, quick and full of ideas, and conversations with them range everywhere. The relationship shifts with life stages: sometimes very close, sometimes each busy with their own life. {{B:天機:When Tian Ji is strong, your exchanges are lively and they help you find solutions.|When Tian Ji is weak, your ideas often clash and contact tends to be less steady.}}`,scenes:[`You mention you want to buy a car, and your brother sends five comparison sites and three payment plans.`,`You and a business partner come up with new ideas at every meeting, and the plan reaches its seventh draft before any work starts.`],advice:`Once you have heard everyone's suggestions, set a deadline; an idea only counts once it lands.`},
'天機·太陰':{title:`A window for sharing secrets on moonlit nights`,story:`Your siblings or peers are gentle, perceptive and sensitive; your interactions lean toward heart-to-hearts and looking out for each other, and sisters or female peers often have a particularly strong influence. The relationship changes with moves, studies and jobs, and you may live in different cities. The friction is that you are both sensitive, and a single remark can play on your mind for a long time.`,scenes:[`When you are feeling low, your younger sister texts "how have you been lately?" and it brings a lump to your throat.`,`You may spend a whole day quietly wondering if you said something wrong because your cousin did not reply in the group chat.`],advice:`If something feels off, just ask; it takes far less energy than guessing all night.`},
'天機·巨門':{title:`A family debate club that never adjourns`,story:`Your siblings or peers are sharp and articulate; you can talk deeply and you can also bicker endlessly. When your views differ, you argue it all the way through, and misunderstandings usually come from speaking too fast. They can help you take a problem apart, but their criticism does not spare your feelings.`,scenes:[`At a family dinner the talk turns to house prices, and you and your brother argue from the starters until dessert arrives.`,`You and a business partner may write long debates in a chat about one detail, only to realize at the end that you basically agree.`],advice:`Before you start arguing, check that you are actually discussing the same thing; many fights will not need to happen.`},
'天機·天梁':{title:`An older sibling who loves giving advice`,story:`Your siblings or close peers are worldly and analytical and often play the role of adviser and caretaker. There may be an age gap between you, or one of you grew up especially fast. The help: there is always someone with an idea when trouble hits. The friction: it can sound preachy, as if you are being lectured.`,scenes:[`You say you want to quit without a job lined up and go travelling, and your sister first sends you an article about insurance and emergency funds.`,`You may be the one peers call to settle disputes, spending weekends on the phone listening to other people's troubles.`],advice:`Before giving advice, ask: "Do you want me to listen, or do you want ideas?"`},
'太陽':{title:`The lamp that lights the whole family`,story:`Your siblings or peers are warm, generous and loyal, and brothers or male peers have an especially noticeable influence. Between you, helping each other is the norm and giving outweighs keeping score. {{B:太陽:With Tai Yang strong, you give each other a lot of support and the relationship is open and bright.|With Tai Yang weak, you may give more without being noticed, or one of your siblings may be having a harder time.}}`,scenes:[`When your younger brother moves, you lend him your car without a second thought and help carry furniture until midnight.`,`You may often be the one who pays when your friends get together; everyone says they will pay you back, and you always say you will sort it out next time.`],advice:`Stay warm-hearted, but before you jump in, check how much fuel is left in your own tank.`},
'太陽·太陰':{title:`A family cared for by sun and moon in shifts`,story:`Your siblings or peers combine strength and softness: you may have both brothers and sisters, or one person who runs hot and cold. The relationship has real warmth, but also visible emotional ups and downs. Different people step in to help you at different times, and friction often comes from mismatched expectations.`,scenes:[`When something comes up at home, your brother handles the paperwork during the day and your sister keeps your mother company in the evening.`,`You might talk to your sister on the phone every day for a while, then go a month without contact.`],advice:`You do not need everyone to care for you in the same way; each person's light counts.`},
'太陽·巨門':{title:`A loud family with warm hearts`,story:`Your siblings or peers are passionate and outspoken, and discussions get especially loud. You have plenty of spats, but they are usually about the issue, not the person. With Tai Yang shining on the misunderstandings Ju Men brings, you can usually lay things out and clear them up. You work well together on things that need communication and self-expression.`,scenes:[`The family group chat erupts over who takes your parents to their medical appointments, and you still end up with a rotation schedule.`,`You may partner with a peer in teaching or sales and build the business by being willing to speak up.`],advice:`After an argument, remember to close the loop; a simple "I was too harsh just now" saves a lot.`},
'太陽·天梁':{title:`Siblings who grew up under one big tree`,story:`Your siblings or peers have an elder's bearing, warm and loyal, with a strong sense of looking after one another. You may be the one being cared for, or the one who carries everyone. The help: someone will always hold you up in hard times. The friction: they care so much that they cannot resist meddling in each other's lives.`,scenes:[`When you are in hospital for a few days, your brother takes leave to stay with you and tells you to give up late-night snacks while he is at it.`,`You may be the peer who regularly polishes people's resumes and introduces them to jobs.`],advice:`Leave some space alongside the caring; it is fine to let them stumble once on their own.`},
'武曲':{title:`Steel-willed siblings who keep accounts clear`,story:`Your siblings or peers are upright and practical, valuing action over sweet words; you keep a sense of proportion and clear lines around money. The Siblings palace also reflects cash flow, and Wu Qu here reminds you to plan your own ready money. {{B:武曲:When Wu Qu is strong, you can back each other up financially.|When Wu Qu is weak, you more often each manage your own affairs.}}`,scenes:[`When you and your sister buy a fridge for your parents together, she sends a spreadsheet showing exactly what each of you owes.`,`You may run a small business with a peer; they work hard and dependably, but are not much for talking about feelings.`],advice:`Appreciate their directness and tell them what you need too; a tough relationship can still have warmth.`},
'武曲·天府':{title:`A guarded family vault`,story:`Your siblings or peers take money seriously and are steady, good at saving and managing it. The help between you is very practical, such as job referrals or short-term loans. The relationship leans toward the rational, and affection is not always spoken aloud. You usually have backup for cash flow, though they will also care how you use the money.`,scenes:[`When you need an emergency loan, your brother agrees quickly but casually asks about your repayment plan.`,`You may manage your parents' savings with your sister, and both of you are careful enough to reconcile every entry.`],advice:`Always write down a repayment schedule; protecting your credit is protecting your relationship.`},
'武曲·天相':{title:`A dependable family finance chief`,story:`Your siblings or peers are down to earth and value trust; they are willing to help but have principles. Your dealings are fair and rarely leave anyone owing a favor. They are the ones who can sort out paperwork and coordinate errands for you. The friction is that there are a lot of rules, and sometimes you feel managed.`,scenes:[`When claiming on your parents' insurance, it is your younger brother who organizes every receipt and form.`,`Sharing a flat with a friend, you may find they split the utilities down to the cent.`],advice:`Set the rules up front, and you will be each other's easiest collaborators.`},
'武曲·七殺':{title:`Two swords, each sharpened alone`,story:`Your siblings or peers are tough, independent and decisive. You rarely fuss over each other; you each fight your own battles. Partnerships are highly efficient, but disagreements can turn into head-on clashes. Cash flow mostly depends on yourself, and lending and borrowing between you is especially prone to friction.`,scenes:[`When the old family house needs renovating, you settle on a contractor in three days and have one big fight along the way.`,`You may start a business with a peer, race ahead for six months, and then reach a standoff over how to split the profits.`],advice:`Put responsibilities in writing before working together; the tougher the people, the more they need rules.`},
'武曲·破軍':{title:`An expedition that sets off on a whim`,story:`Your siblings or peers dare to charge ahead, spend and switch tracks, and the relationship swings a lot; for a while you may each be building lives in different places. Money between you comes with many variables, so leave extra buffer in your cash flow. The upside is that when things shift, their drive can give you a push.`,scenes:[`Your cousin suddenly announces a working holiday in Australia and borrows the airfare from you before leaving.`,`You may open a shop with a peer and see the renovation costs come in at double the budget.`],advice:`Lend only what you can afford, capping it at an amount whose loss would not affect your life.`},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:`Companions who know how to earn and how to play`,story:`Your siblings or peers have a nose for money and know how to enjoy life. You might run a small business together or chase a shared hobby. When the mood is good you can talk about anything, but dividing up gains easily turns into keeping score. You may not have had much contact early on, and grow closer as the years go by.`,scenes:[`You and your brother run a market stall together, and after a profitable weekend you go out for a big barbecue dinner.`,`When friends organize a group purchase, you are the one who haggles and also collects and splits the money.`],advice:`Split the money you earn together on the same day, and the good times can last.`},
'天同':{title:`A family chatting around a hot pot`,story:`Your siblings or peers are gentle and easy to be around; nobody keeps score, things are relaxed, and there is more companionship than demands. The help is emotional support; the friction is that when something needs doing, everyone waits for someone else. {{B:天同:When Tian Tong is strong, the family is harmonious and easy together.|When Tian Tong is weak, each of you may carry private worries, staying pleasant on the surface but rarely talking deeply.}}`,scenes:[`Family gatherings have no big agenda; you just eat, watch variety shows and laugh until you cry.`,`You may agree with your siblings to clear out the family home together, and three months later nobody has started.`],advice:`Being relaxed is a blessing; for important matters, remember to name a person in charge and a date.`},
'天同·太陰':{title:`A pot of warm tea, slowly brewed`,story:`Your siblings or peers are perceptive and tender, with lots of emotional exchange, and sisters or female peers are especially thoughtful. You rarely have fierce conflicts, but moods easily spread between you. The help is that someone understands how you feel; the friction is being so considerate of each other that many things go unsaid.`,scenes:[`The night of your breakup, your younger sister shows up with fried chicken and binge-watches a whole series with you.`,`Because you feel awkward turning down your cousin's request, your whole weekend gets taken up again.`],advice:`Alongside the gentleness, practice saying "no"; the relationship will not go cold because of it.`},
'天同·巨門':{title:`A dinner table full of unspoken feelings`,story:`Your siblings or peers are emotionally rich, but communication often gets stuck on misunderstandings. On the surface all is well, but small grievances may be hidden, and left too long they turn into a cold war. The help is that you can complain and unwind together; the friction is that things only ever get half said.`,scenes:[`Nobody says it out loud, but you are all quietly keeping track of who does more for your parents.`,`You make a joke in the group chat, the other person does not reply, and days later you find out they were quietly upset.`],advice:`If something is bothering you, talk it through early; the longer it drags, the harder it is to fix.`},
'天同·天梁':{title:`A big family where someone always has your back`,story:`Your siblings or peers are kind and caring, with a sense of older ones supporting younger ones. Your relationship is stable and warm, and when hard times come, someone often steps in without being asked. The friction is leaning on each other too much, or the same person always carrying more.`,scenes:[`When you are too busy to get away, your sister picks your child up from school and makes sure they are fed.`,`You may be the one in your circle often invited to dinner who ends up listening to someone pour their heart out all night.`],advice:`When you are cared for, remember to give back; when you care for others, remember to leave time to rest.`},
'廉貞':{title:`Companions who love and hate wholeheartedly`,story:`Your siblings or peers have strong characters and principles, with intense feelings but clear boundaries. You may clash over values, yet deep down you admire each other. Lian Zhen brings a competitive edge, and siblings may quietly compare themselves. When something really happens, they will stand by you.`,scenes:[`You and your sister compared grades as kids; as adults you compare jobs, homes and children.`,`You may organize an event with a peer whose insistence makes the result beautiful and the process exhausting.`],advice:`Turn comparison into learning from each other, and both of you will feel much lighter.`},
'廉貞·天府':{title:`A family estate run by the rules`,story:`Your siblings or peers are steady and measured, good at running and managing things. Your interactions follow an order; the relationship is not clingy, but it is very reliable. When money or household issues come up, they handle them calmly and rationally. The friction is that everyone has their own firm views.`,scenes:[`When discussing your parents' retirement arrangements, you divide the work as if in a meeting, with everyone's role crystal clear.`,`You may work with a peer who keeps the accounts immaculate, yet you feel something warm is missing.`],advice:`Add some warmth to the order, and now and then share a meal with no agenda.`},
'廉貞·天相':{title:`The peacemaker always smoothing things over`,story:`Your siblings or peers value loyalty and rules and often act as coordinators and peacemakers. Your relationship is strongly shaped by circumstances, and big family events ripple through all of you. The help: someone handles the tedious stuff for you. The friction: it often comes down to rules or saving face.`,scenes:[`When relatives fall out, your cousin is always the one who mediates and even keeps a tidy record of the conversations.`,`You may sign a lease with a good friend who cares far more than you do about every penalty clause.`],advice:`Thank the person who is always mediating, and do not let them carry everything alone.`},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:`A squad charging into battle`,story:`Your siblings or peers are decisive and driven; you all have strong personalities, interactions are blunt, and sparks are bound to fly. Working together you can achieve real results, but in an argument harsh words come easily. When real trouble hits, they are comrades who will fight alongside you.`,scenes:[`You and your brother take your parents abroad, pack every day with plans, and everyone comes home exhausted and thinner.`,`You may win a project together with a peer, then argue over who gets the credit at the celebration dinner.`],advice:`Spell out your shared goal first, and drive will not turn into infighting.`},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:`A family drama that keeps rewriting its script`,story:`Your siblings or peers have strong personalities and love adventure; the relationship has clear ups and downs and may come together and drift apart, or you may each go on to very different lives. Partnerships need extra attention to unknowns, and you should leave room in your cash flow. The upside is that they often show you new possibilities.`,scenes:[`Your younger sister suddenly decides to move abroad, and the family holds several meetings about it.`,`You may work with a friend on a plan, and halfway through they suggest scrapping it all and starting over.`],advice:`Stay flexible when working with them, while holding on to your own bottom line.`},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:`Playmates who love the night`,story:`Your siblings or peers are socially skilled and love a lively scene, living colorful lives. Much of your time together happens at gatherings and entertainment, and when things are good you can talk about anything. Friction is mostly about spending, social circles or boundaries; the wilder the fun, the more carefully you need to track the bill.`,scenes:[`Your brother takes you to a concert, you go on somewhere afterward, and you get home at three in the morning.`,`At a friends' gathering you may get egged on into paying for everyone, and regret it the next day when the card alert arrives.`],advice:`Set a budget before going out together; have a great time and still protect your wallet.`},
'天府':{title:`A reliable neighbor beside the granary`,story:`Your siblings or peers are steady, tolerant and good at preserving what they have, and you get along peacefully. The help between you is very practical, such as caring for family members or stepping in with a loan when needed. The relationship is not passionate, but it is reliable over the long term. The friction is that they are more conservative and not keen on taking risks.`,scenes:[`You say you want to quit and start a business; your sister supports you, but first reminds you to save six months of living costs.`,`You may be used to your brother organizing every holiday gathering, with everyone else just showing up.`],advice:`Treasure this stability, and share your plans with them so they can feel at ease.`},
'太陰':{title:`Soft moonlight by the window`,story:`Your siblings or peers are gentle and perceptive, and sisters or female friends have a more noticeable influence. Your interactions are on the quiet side, with care hidden in small gestures. {{B:太陰:When Tai Yin is strong, you are close to each other and your bond is stable.|When Tai Yin is weak, the relationship is cooler, or moods easily lead to misunderstandings.}}`,scenes:[`On your birthday your sister makes no big fuss, but sends you a box of the cookies you loved as a child.`,`A careless remark from your cousin may leave you hurt for days.`],advice:`Sensitivity is a strength; say so when you are hurt, so they have a chance to make it right.`},
'貪狼':{title:`Fun-loving, talented companions`,story:`Your siblings or peers are multitalented and sociable, and time together is fun and lively, though there may be some comparison: who is more popular, who earns more. The help is that they introduce you to new circles; the friction lies in spending and temptation.`,scenes:[`Your younger brother pulls you into his board game club, where you meet the person who is now your business partner.`,`You may chase hobbies together with a peer, from camping to photography, buying the full kit for each.`],advice:`Enjoy the buzz they bring, and stay clear about what you yourself really want.`},
'巨門':{title:`A door that never quite shuts`,story:`Your siblings or peers are expressive and observant, but communication often stalls, with misunderstandings mostly coming from tone or secondhand messages. The upside is that they analyze well and dare to question, helping you see your own blind spots. As long as you are willing to talk things through, the relationship is not hard to mend.`,scenes:[`At a family gathering, one "you've put on weight lately" is enough to spoil your appetite for the whole evening.`,`You may work with a partner who questions every expense; it is annoying, but it genuinely saves you money.`],advice:`Say important things face to face; do not let messages and go-betweens interpret for you.`},
'天相':{title:`The one always handing you an umbrella`,story:`Your siblings or peers are kind, polite and willing to help, often playing the role of supporter and coordinator. Your relationship is peaceful and respectful. The help: someone takes care of details and handles people for you. The friction: everyone is so polite that real thoughts stay hidden.`,scenes:[`When you move, your cousin quietly writes you a packing list and books the movers.`,`You may get caught in the middle when two friends fall out, with both coming to you to vent.`],advice:`Add a bit more frankness to the politeness, and the relationship will feel more genuine.`},
'天梁':{title:`The old shade tree at the front door`,story:`Your siblings or peers are mature and caring, often acting as elders or protectors; there may be a big age gap, or one of you grew up especially fast. {{B:天梁:When Tian Liang is strong, their protection is strong and someone has your back when things go wrong.|When Tian Liang is weak, the caring comes mixed with nagging that leaves you a little short of breath.}}`,scenes:[`Before you change jobs, your brother has already compared the benefits and promotion paths at three companies for you.`,`You may be the peer everyone calls to fix problems, with your phone often ringing in the middle of the night.`],advice:`Say thank you when you are looked after, and gently let them know you have grown up.`},
'七殺':{title:`Two sentries, each at their own post`,story:`Your siblings or peers are independent and decisive, each with their own battlefield. You do not spend much time together, but you back each other up when something big happens. Working together is efficient, though disagreements can turn into head-on clashes. Cash flow leans toward self-reliance, with little dependence on family.`,scenes:[`When the family has to decide whether to sell the old house, you settle it in one meeting, though the air crackles throughout.`,`You may work with a friend who moves fast and sharp, and you have to pick up the pace to keep up.`],advice:`Respect each other's independence, and agree to keep in regular touch so you do not drift apart.`},
'破軍':{title:`A journey of constant moving house`,story:`Your siblings or peers have vivid personalities and love change, and the relationship moves between close and distant; you may live in different cities or head in very different directions in life. Leave room for change in partnerships, and do not lean too heavily on others for cash flow. The upside is that they give you the courage to break old molds.`,scenes:[`Your sister changes jobs four times in three years, saying each time, "This time it's definitely right."`,`You may open a studio with an old friend, then six months later, as your ideas change, part ways amicably.`],advice:`Treat change as their normal, and simply keep your own rhythm.`},
'空':{title:`A mirror reflecting the opposite palace`,story:`Your Siblings palace has no main star, so relationships with siblings and peers are read through the main stars of the opposite palace, Friends, and are strongly shaped by circumstance and life stage. Your connection with siblings is very flexible: close in one period, distant in another. Where you are and who is around you often decides what the relationship looks like.`,scenes:[`As a child you barely spoke to your brother, but once you both worked in the same city you became good friends.`,`You may change jobs or move house, and the peers you see most get replaced as a whole group.`],advice:`Actively choose the people you want to be close to; you can shape what your relationships look like.`}
},
'僕役':{
'紫微':{title:`Friends who all want to be the lead`,story:`With Zi Wei in your Friends palace, your friends tend to have status and ability, and your network sits at a fairly high level. But capable friends and staff do not necessarily take your orders; sometimes you end up following them. The help: there are people in your circle with real influence. The friction: who leads and who gives way.`,scenes:[`The new hire you are training is very capable and often proposes directions completely different from yours in meetings.`,`At a class reunion you may find everyone has become a manager or a boss, and chatting feels like a board meeting.`],advice:`Share the stage and give strong people room to shine, and they will become your support.`},
'紫微·天府':{title:`A card holder full of VIPs`,story:`Your circle of friends is high level, steady and capable, with plenty of resources. Your dealings are about the big picture and mutual benefit, with little pointless small talk. The help is that your network brings real opportunities; the friction is that everyone has their own ideas and will not necessarily follow your pace.`,scenes:[`A senior figure you met at a dinner introduces you to a major client six months later.`,`You may manage a strong team where everyone has their own way of doing things, and coordinating matters more than giving orders.`],advice:`Building a network is about long-term mutual benefit; do not only get in touch when you need a favor.`},
'紫微·天相':{title:`A dinner party where etiquette matters`,story:`Your friends and colleagues care about image and manners, and your dealings are always proper. In your circles you are often expected to look after the bigger picture and keep things steady. The help: people are willing to make introductions and vouch for you. The friction: everything is harmonious on the surface while everyone has private calculations.`,scenes:[`At the company year-end dinner you are seated at the managers' table and spend the whole evening making conversation and toasts.`,`You may introduce two friends to work together, they do not get along, and you end up in the middle calming both sides.`],advice:`Get to know both sides before making an introduction; you are not fully responsible for every relationship.`},
'紫微·破軍':{title:`An expedition that keeps changing members`,story:`Your friends tend to be individualistic and adventurous, and your social circle changes a lot: one group in this stage, a different one in the next. Your staff are capable but hard to manage and may come and go. The help is that you meet people from new fields and your horizons keep opening.`,scenes:[`You join a startup community, and a year later half the core members have changed.`,`You may have managed a very capable team member who achieved great results and then went off to start their own business.`],advice:`Accept that people come and go, and make the most of each collaboration while it lasts.`},
'紫微·七殺':{title:`Generals, each with their own territory`,story:`Your friends and colleagues have strong personalities, real ability and decisiveness. You respect each other, but there is plenty of tug-of-war over power. The help: when a tough fight comes, someone can hold the line. The friction: nobody wants to be told what to do, so meetings easily become contests of strength.`,scenes:[`Everyone on the project team is strong, and the first meeting turns into an hour-long argument over who does what.`,`You may make a friend who speaks very bluntly, yet is the first to call when you are at your lowest.`],advice:`Explain the goal to strong people rather than giving orders, and you will get real cooperation in return.`},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:`A star-studded party`,story:`Your friends are multitalented, love having fun, are socially skilled and know lots of people. Your life is often lively thanks to friends, and social engagements multiply. The friction is around spending, time and boundaries; you need to tell true friends apart from people you just drink with.`,scenes:[`You get invited out three evenings a week and are shocked by the credit card bill at the end of the month.`,`At a gathering you may meet the mentor who helps you change careers, and also someone who only ever comes to you to borrow money.`],advice:`Give your time first to the friends who really matter; alongside the buzz, make room for deeper friendships.`},
'天機':{title:`A crowd of quick-witted idea people`,story:`Your friends are clever and well informed, and conversations are rich. Your social circle often changes with your environment: a new job means a new group of friends. {{B:天機:When Tian Ji is strong, your network is nimble and there is always someone to offer ideas or look things up for you.|When Tian Ji is weak, you have plenty of contacts but few close ones, and joint plans tend to fizzle out halfway.}}`,scenes:[`You ask the group chat for a good dentist and within ten minutes get ten recommendations and three comparison articles.`,`You and a colleague may agree on a side project together, discuss it eagerly, then both get busy and it goes nowhere.`],advice:`From the crowd of clever people, pick one or two who are willing to see things through with you.`},
'天機·太陰':{title:`A long letter to an old friend`,story:`Your friends are perceptive, gentle and thoughtful; you prefer a few close friends to many, and female friends or colleagues often look out for you especially. Friendships often shift with moves and job changes, but the truly good friends stay. The friction is that you are both sensitive, and misunderstandings are not easily cleared up.`,scenes:[`Years after you left a job, a former colleague still sometimes sends photos of the café you used to go to together.`,`You might spend days privately wondering whether you were left out because friends got together without inviting you.`],advice:`Treasure friendships that flow slowly and steadily, and reach out when you have doubts.`},
'天機·巨門':{title:`A spirited book club`,story:`Your friends are clever and articulate, enjoy debate and analysis, and your exchanges go deep, often sparking each other's thinking. Friction comes from verbal clashes and misunderstandings; be careful with talk behind people's backs and secondhand messages.`,scenes:[`You and your friends discuss current events until you are red in the face, then go out for breakfast together the next day.`,`You may lead a team that is good at asking questions, where every proposal has to survive several rounds of challenges before it is settled.`],advice:`Appreciate their questioning, and agree together on a rule of debating the issue, not the person.`},
'天機·天梁':{title:`Old friends who love playing consultant`,story:`Your friends are knowledgeable and love giving advice, and there are plenty of older or more experienced people around you. Your interactions feel like consulting each other, and you each learn from the other. The help: someone gives you pointers when trouble arises. The friction: too much advice, and a somewhat preachy tone.`,scenes:[`You float a business idea and your friends take turns doing a risk assessment for you.`,`You may be the person new hires ask most, hearing "how should I handle this?" ten times a day.`],advice:`After hearing the advice, make your own judgment; do not let opinions drown out your decision.`},
'太陽':{title:`The lamp that lights the whole team`,story:`Your friends are warm and generous, and you are often the giver in your relationships, with male friends or colleagues offering more noticeable help. {{B:太陽:When Tai Yang is strong, people like you, and what you give comes back to you.|When Tai Yang is weak, your eagerness to help may go unremembered, and it can easily wear you out.}}`,scenes:[`When a colleague works late, you go out to buy them dinner and stay until they finish.`,`You may lend money to a friend in need, and afterward they rarely mention it again.`],advice:`Be generous, but choose who you give to, and let your kindness flow to those who value it.`},
'太陽·太陰':{title:`Partners working day and night shifts`,story:`Your friends include men and women, the passionate and the gentle, and your circle is quite diverse. Your social life rises and falls with your mood and stage of life: sometimes very active, sometimes you just want quiet. Different kinds of friends become your support at different times.`,scenes:[`By day you have lively discussions in meetings with colleagues; by night you have quiet heart-to-hearts with old friends in a small bar.`,`You may love going to events for a while, then want nothing but time alone for the next stretch.`],advice:`Accept your own social rhythm; there is no need to force every phase to be equally lively.`},
'太陽·巨門':{title:`A busy radio station`,story:`Your friends are passionate and talkative, and information travels fast in your circle. You make a great team for promotion, marketing or teaching, with loud voices and wide reach. The friction is gossip; words passed from person to person easily get distorted, and even a joke can be taken seriously.`,scenes:[`You casually complain once in a group chat, and by the next day the whole department knows.`,`You may team up with friends on livestreams or talks and draw a regular audience with your speaking skills.`],advice:`Before you speak, think about whose ears it will reach, and use your eloquence in the right places.`},
'太陽·天梁':{title:`A big tree people rest under`,story:`Your friends are loyal and have a sense of justice; in your circles you are often seen as someone to rely on, and there is no shortage of warm-hearted elders and mentors around you. The help is mutual support; the friction is that you may manage and care for too much and stretch yourself thin.`,scenes:[`Friends often ask you to settle their disputes, and you end up knowing every detail of their family affairs.`,`You may be the one in the department quietly mentoring new hires, still answering questions after work.`],advice:`Caring for others needs boundaries too; learn to say "try this one yourself first."`},
'武曲':{title:`A team of efficient doers`,story:`Your friends are practical and direct, and your dealings mostly involve work or money. Your relationships are about balancing interests, and you do not spend much time nurturing feelings. {{B:武曲:When Wu Qu is strong, your network brings real opportunities.|When Wu Qu is weak, money can easily cause friction in your dealings.}}`,scenes:[`You and a friend take on a project together, and the first thing they ask is how the pay will be split.`,`You may manage staff who work efficiently but rarely chat, leaving the team atmosphere on the cool side.`],advice:`Beyond being clear about interests, treat everyone to a meal now and then; relationships need investment too.`},
'武曲·天府':{title:`Old friends with solid means`,story:`Your friends are financially stable and dependable, and your network brings resources and opportunities. Your dealings rest on trust, and relationships usually last a long time. The friction is that everyone leans conservative, so pushing new ideas takes a lot of effort.`,scenes:[`When you cannot find a venue for an event, an old friend simply lends you his company's meeting room.`,`You may manage a very stable team, but introducing a new system meets considerable resistance.`],advice:`Treasure this reliability, and when pushing something new, spend more time persuading people.`},
'武曲·天相':{title:`Good teammates who play by the rules`,story:`Your friends and colleagues are dependable and trustworthy, and willing to help you. Your dealings are fair and seldom leave favors owing. The friction is a strong focus on rules; when flexibility is needed they are not adaptable enough, and last-minute changes make everyone uneasy.`,scenes:[`When the team divides up the work, everyone turns in their part on time and nobody needs chasing.`,`You may ask a friend to look over a contract, and they annotate it clause by clause, even circling the typos.`],advice:`Turn trust into an easy understanding, and now and then give each other a little room to flex.`},
'武曲·七殺':{title:`A well-disciplined troop`,story:`Your friends are strong-willed and decisive, and your dealings are direct and to the point. You can accomplish tough tasks together, and in conflicts you meet head-on. Your staff are capable but need clear instructions and goals to perform well; the clearer your direction, the harder they push.`,scenes:[`During a project crunch everyone stays up late together, then argues over one decision until someone pounds the table.`,`You may become close friends with someone you met at the gym, a friendship built on sweating together.`],advice:`Make the rules and goals clear; a tough team fights best that way.`},
'武曲·破軍':{title:`Adventurers who scatter as fast as they gather`,story:`Your friends are bold and love adventure, and your social circle changes a lot. Money is often involved in your dealings, so be especially careful with loans and partnerships. The upside is that they introduce you to new fields and show you opportunities you would never otherwise have touched.`,scenes:[`A friend invites you to co-invest in a restaurant with great enthusiasm, and six months later everyone has pulled out.`,`You may have had a team member who was great at hitting sales targets, but whose methods often skirted the edge of the rules.`],advice:`Always keep paperwork for money matters, no matter how close the friendship.`},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:`Talking business over dinner`,story:`Your friends know how to make money and how to enjoy it, and social life and business often blend together. Your network brings opportunities, but also a lot of wining and dining. Friction comes from splitting profits and costs; who should pay how much is often too awkward to say. With them, the danger is not arguing but silently keeping score.`,scenes:[`Casual chat during a round of golf leads to a business deal.`,`You may organize a group trip with friends, and after you get back there is always someone whose share never quite gets settled.`],advice:`Keep separate accounts for socializing and business, so you can have fun and still keep things clear.`},
'天同':{title:`Old friends who join you for late-night snacks`,story:`Your friends are gentle and easy to get along with; you are well liked, and relationships are relaxed. There are few conflicts of interest between you, mostly companionship and sharing. {{B:天同:When Tian Tong is strong, you have many friends and warm friendships.|When Tian Tong is weak, the friendships are good, but there is less practical help when you really need it.}} Everyone is easygoing, so things also tend to get put off again and again.`,scenes:[`One phone call on a Friday night is all it takes to find someone to go out for street food with you.`,`You may agree with friends to lose weight together, and three months later everyone has gained a few pounds.`],advice:`Easy friendships are precious; when you need to keep each other on track, say so.`},
'天同·太陰':{title:`A warm little café`,story:`Your friends are gentle and perceptive, and female friends or colleagues are especially thoughtful. Your exchanges lean toward emotional support and looking out for each other. The friction is that nobody likes conflict, so things get bottled up, and over time that builds distance.`,scenes:[`When you take sick leave, a colleague quietly organizes your work and leaves a note on your desk.`,`You may be very close to a friend yet never manage to ask for the book you lent them back.`],advice:`Be direct as well as gentle; say what you need.`},
'天同·巨門':{title:`A break room with a delicate atmosphere`,story:`Your friends are friendly on the surface, but small misunderstandings and gossip easily arise in private, so watch out for hearsay and talk behind backs. The upside is that you can always find someone willing to listen and share a good vent with you. Just take any news you hear with a pinch of salt before believing it.`,scenes:[`You casually grumble about your manager in the break room, and a few days later the version you hear back is completely distorted.`,`You may have a group of colleagues to vent with, and dinners after work are livelier than the workday itself.`],advice:`Venting is fine, but say important things only to people you trust.`},
'天同·天梁':{title:`Old neighbors who look out for each other`,story:`Your friends are kind and warm-hearted, there is a strong spirit of mutual help, and someone always reaches out when you are in trouble. The friction is relying on each other too much, or you always being the one who looks after others, so busy that you forget you need looking after too.`,scenes:[`You go abroad for ten days, and friends water your plants, collect your mail and feed your cat without being asked.`,`You may be the most helpful person in the neighborhood group chat, even the one who reposts the water outage notices.`],advice:`Make mutual help go both ways; you do not have to be the first to give every time.`},
'廉貞':{title:`A circle that loves and hates wholeheartedly`,story:`Your friends have strong personalities and intense friendships, but may also fall out over differing values. Workplace relationships carry a competitive edge, and colleagues may quietly compare themselves. The help: someone stands by you at crucial moments. The friction: relationships easily swing to extremes.`,scenes:[`You and a friend give each other the cold shoulder for six months over something small, then make up after an unexpected event.`,`You may sense colleagues quietly competing at the office, with the atmosphere especially tense before promotions are announced.`],advice:`Look at values first when making friends, and do not insist that everyone like you.`},
'廉貞·天府':{title:`A guild with clear rules`,story:`Your friends are capable and business-minded, and your network leans professional and career-focused. Your dealings are orderly and practical; relationships are stable but not clingy. The friction is that everyone has their own views, so cooperation takes time to settle, and negotiating terms often takes longer than doing the work.`,scenes:[`At an industry networking event, everyone you meet has a clear collaboration goal in mind.`,`You may manage a well-disciplined team, but sparking creativity takes extra effort.`],advice:`Leave a little room for the human touch within the rules, and cooperation will go much more smoothly.`},
'廉貞·天相':{title:`A web that needs careful upkeep`,story:`Your friends value loyalty and rules; your relationships are strongly shaped by circumstances and systems, and you are often the coordinator in a group. The help: someone is willing to step forward for you. The friction: disputes often arise from unclear rules or misunderstandings.`,scenes:[`When your club holds an event, you are made the point of contact and everyone's opinions land on you to sort out.`,`You may agree to act as a guarantor or vouch for a friend, then find out afterward the responsibility is bigger than you thought.`],advice:`Coordinating is fine, but think twice about anything involving your signature or a guarantee.`},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:`Comrades fighting side by side`,story:`Your friends are bold and willing to fight hard, and your friendships are mostly built through struggling together. Working together you are full of drive, and in conflict things get heated. Your staff are capable but need time to sync with your rhythm; get through the first three months and the teamwork clicks.`,scenes:[`You and a colleague survive a difficult client together and become close friends from then on.`,`You may have an opinionated team member who executes brilliantly but often ignores the process.`],advice:`A shared goal is your best glue; align your direction before setting off.`},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:`A band that keeps changing its lineup`,story:`Your friends have strong personalities and love adventure; your social circle changes a lot and relationships can run hot and cold. Collaborations are full of unknowns, and trust and commitment take time to prove. The upside is that you meet all kinds of people, and life is rarely boring.`,scenes:[`The club you belong to changes its committee every year, and the rules change dramatically with it.`,`You may work with a friend on a plan, they change their mind halfway, and you have to find someone else.`],advice:`Have a backup for important collaborations, and do not stake success or failure on a single person.`},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:`A brightly lit social circle`,story:`Your friends are highly social and know how to have fun, and your social life is full of engagements and parties. Your network brings opportunities and also temptations. Friction is mostly about spending, boundaries and tangled relationships. While enjoying yourself, you also need to tell who really cares about you.`,scenes:[`A friend pulls you into a new circle, and from then on there is a party invitation every week.`,`You may have so many social engagements that you cannot keep a single full weekend for yourself.`],advice:`Be selective about what you attend, and save your time for people who help you grow.`},
'天府':{title:`A sturdy granary of connections`,story:`Your friends are steady and tolerant; your social circle may not be large, but it is very reliable. Friends and staff mostly do their part and help you protect what you have achieved. The friction is that everyone leans conservative, so warming up to trying new things together takes a while.`,scenes:[`When you hit a rough patch, a friend of ten years connects you with resources without a second thought.`,`You may lead a team where hardly anyone leaves; the teamwork is great, but the response to change is slow.`],advice:`Treasure old friends, and meet some new people too, to keep the granary fresh.`},
'太陰':{title:`A gentle gathering under the moon`,story:`Your friends are gentle and perceptive, and female friends or colleagues offer more noticeable help. You prefer a few close friends to many, and value emotional connection. {{B:太陰:When Tai Yin is strong, your friends are thoughtful and your friendships are warm.|When Tai Yin is weak, your relationships are cooler, and sensitivity can easily create distance.}}`,scenes:[`You do not have many close friends, but every one of them knows which bakery's cake is your favorite.`,`You may be quiet at group events, then message one friend privately afterward to share your thoughts.`],advice:`Reach out to the people you care about; quiet friendships need watering too.`},
'貪狼':{title:`A party that never runs short of guests`,story:`You have many friends and a wide social reach, and there is always a buzz around you. Your network brings opportunities, along with temptations and social obligations. The friction lies in telling who is sincere and who is just there for the fun; the depth of a friendship takes time to reveal.`,scenes:[`You have over a thousand contacts in your phone, yet only two or three you could call in the middle of the night.`,`At a gathering a friend may bring you into a new circle that changes the direction of your life.`],advice:`As you widen your network, keep an eye on who your real friends are.`},
'巨門':{title:`A meeting room with a big echo`,story:`Your friends are articulate and observant, but gossip and disputes come up easily, and misunderstandings with friends and colleagues mostly come down to communication. The upside is that they help you see problems and offer ideas you had not thought of; if you can take it on board, that is real help.`,scenes:[`You present a plan in a meeting, and a colleague immediately fires off ten questions.`,`A friend may misread something you said, and it takes weeks of tension before you clear it up.`],advice:`Say important things face to face, then confirm them in writing, and rely less on secondhand messages.`},
'天相':{title:`A team of reliable helpers`,story:`Your friends and colleagues are kind, courteous and willing to help; you easily find support in your relationships and often act as the coordinator. The friction is that everyone cares so much about harmony that problems rarely get named, and the longer they drag on, the harder they are to handle.`,scenes:[`When you are swamped, a colleague offers, "Want me to take care of this report for you?"`,`You may play peacemaker among friends while keeping your own views hidden.`],advice:`Build harmony on honesty; once the truth is out, the relationship becomes steadier.`},
'天梁':{title:`Friends who feel like elders`,story:`Your friends are mature and caring; older, more experienced people often give you a hand, and you may also be the one looking after others. {{B:天梁:When Tian Liang is strong, you have many mentors and plenty of support.|When Tian Liang is weak, the care comes with a bit of burden or lecturing.}}`,scenes:[`When your career stalls, a senior colleague invites you for coffee and helps you sort out your direction.`,`You may be the "head of the family" in your circle of friends, the first one everyone asks when something comes up.`],advice:`Accept care and remember to give back; mentors and those they help lift each other up.`},
'七殺':{title:`Warriors each heading out on their own campaign`,story:`Your friends are independent and decisive, each with their own goals. Your friendships are not about seeing each other every day but about having each other's backs at critical moments. Your staff are capable but not easy to rein in, used to judging for themselves before acting. Give them space and they will give you results.`,scenes:[`You and your best friend only meet twice a year, but when something happens to you, they are the first to call.`,`You may lead team members who are very bold, often starting work before they have even reported in.`],advice:`Use trust instead of control; strong people need a stage, not reins.`},
'破軍':{title:`A revolving door, always opening and closing`,story:`Friends come and go and your social circle changes a lot; you may make completely different types of friends at different stages. Staff turnover tends to be high, and working relationships change quickly too. The upside is that you keep meeting new people and new perspectives, and rarely stagnate.`,scenes:[`After graduating you drift apart from college friends, then meet a like-minded group at your new job.`,`You may manage a team where half the members are new each year, so training people is part of daily life.`],advice:`No need to hold on to everyone; make the most of each encounter.`},
'空':{title:`A mirror borrowing light from the opposite palace`,story:`Your Friends palace has no main star, so your social life is read through the main stars of the opposite palace, Siblings, and is strongly shaped by your environment. Your circle of friends is very flexible: change your surroundings and you change your crowd, and who is around you mostly depends on where you are at the time. The upside is strong adaptability that lets you fit into different groups.`,scenes:[`You have separate groups of friends from school, work and hobby clubs, and none of them know each other.`,`You may move to a new city and build a new network within three months.`],advice:`Actively choose the people you want to be close to, so your environment does not only shape you; you shape it too.`}
}
});
